       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify going above that limit. Doses this high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and they usually don't work better than 200 mg.\n\nPlease check these points:\n- **Typo or wrong drug:** Did you mean 40 mg or 100 mg? Or is it a different medication?\n- **Titration plan:** The usual start is 25\u201350 mg daily. It's increased in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least one week, up to a maximum of 200 mg.\n- **Intentional dose:** If your attending or psychiatry really wants a supratherapeutic dose, they should confirm it directly. I'd enter it with a note documenting that approval and the monitoring plan.\n\nTell me the dose you want, for example \"sertraline 50 mg PO once daily,\" and I'll enter it right away."
